{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792935275,"nonce":"0EUA1qw6N0ILTZ+x5kbdNaLH/yE=","title":"cbproj: workspaces of several projects","message":"Part of 5ed625d51a511b21c35b0b711cf6ddb898831a2fa7bccabc1ecf3bb1973d123a (the project format RayDE opens).\n\nA game, its shared library and its tools are separate projects that belong\ntogether, as ChimpMonk's engine, editor and examples are. This mirrors\nrayzor.toml's workspace:\n\n```toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"game\", \"tools/editor\"]\n```\n\n- **The root file.** A root `.cbproj` may hold only `[workspace]`, or\n  `[workspace]` beside a `[project]` of its own.\n- **Members.** Each member is a directory with exactly one `.cbproj`.\n- **Running.** `caribou run` on a workspace runs the root's project, or\n  names the members to choose from.\n- **Resolving.** `caribou project --json` resolves every member, so an IDE\n  picks a document's member by its path (RayDE's b5069a3 is the same gap for\n  rayzor workspaces).\n- **No shared cache.** There is no `[workspace.cache]`: each member keeps\n  its own `target/`.\n- **Not yet.** A member depending on another member's modules comes later.","files":null}]}